<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pim Fortuyn</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1948">1948</a>–<a href="/years/2002">2002</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pim Fortuyn was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> sociologist and politician whose criticism of immigration, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> and the political establishment made him a leading figure in the election campaign of 2002. He was shot dead by an animal-rights activist on 6 May 2002, nine days before the election, in which his party, the Pim Fortuyn List, came second. His rise transformed Dutch politics.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pim-fortuyn.jpg" alt="Pim Fortuyn" width="245" height="330" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Roy Beusker · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pim_Fortuyn_-_May_4.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
